 * Black-Box API Integration Test
 *
 * @target-controller OwnerRestController
 * (src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/OwnerRestController.java)
 * @target-api PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}
 *
 * Auth: /api/** requires a valid JWT (SecurityConfig). Token obtained via real
 * POST /api/auth/login (admin/password).
 *
 * updateOwner() logic (read directly from source):
 * 1. if (!ownerRepository.existsById(ownerId)) return 404
 * 2. owner.setId(ownerId)  <-- path variable id always overwrites any id in the request body
 * 3. ownerRepository.save(owner) -> 200 with saved owner
 *
 * Same Bean Validation caveat as createOwner: no @Valid on the controller method, but Hibernate's
 * automatic JPA Bean Validation (PreUpdate) still fires on save() because spring-boot-starter-validation
 * is on the classpath, so a ConstraintViolationException from @NotBlank/@Pattern surfaces as an
 * uncaught 500, not a 400.
 *
 * No outbound HTTP calls (detect-external-calls): no WireMock stubs required.
 */
